--- A function every return of which is a failure, handed to `revise` as
--- the revision's function, answers a failure of the record's kind: its
--- own answer named no kind, and the compiled program answered `()` where
--- revise's closure took the record — E0308, a program that did not build
--- (Rosetta Code, Mutex: a withdrawal refused when too little is held).
use memory

struct C [n]

fn refused[c, why]
    return error[why, 'demo']

r = revise['parity442.x', C[0], refused, 'no']
log[r.reason]
log[recall['parity442.x', C[7]].n]
